original:
He clasps the crag with crooked hands;
Close to the sun in lonely lands,
Ringed with the azure world, he stands.
The wrinkled sea beneath him crawls;
He watches from his mountain walls,
And like a thunderbolt he falls.

Love is not all: it is not meat nor drink
Nor slumber nor a roof against the rain;
Yet many a man is willing to be lost...

Love is the rose, and the thorn its honest twin;
you cannot hold the bloom and refuse the pain.
The wise cup both, and call the ache a name.

The loudest love is not the truest;
the quiet kind stays after the fireworks fade,
making tea, and meaning it.

The hill does not care who climbs it;
it offers the same wind to the weak and the strong.
What matters is the foot that lifts again.

You are the blacksmith of your own gate;
the hammer is heavy, the iron is cold,
but the shape is yours to make.

They can take the road, not the walker;
the weather, not the will.
Carry the second, and you arrive.

He who conquers others is strong;
he who conquers himself is mighty.
The second war is the one worth winning.

True knowledge is knowing how little you know.
The full cup cannot hold the rain;
the empty one becomes the stream.

Joy and sorrow are one pendulum;
to still it is to still the life.
Swing, and call both by the name of living.

The uncarved block holds every shape;
the carved one, only one.
Stay a little unformed, and remain free.

Yesterday is a letter written in water;
you may read the shape, never the words.
Let it teach, then let it go.

Time is a visitor who never knocks;
it enters, rearranges the room, and leaves
without taking back a single thing.

A dream is a ladder leaned against the sky;
each step is small, the height is earned.
Do not count the rungs; climb them.

A dream is a compass that points through fog;
you may not see the land, but the needle is true.
Trust the small red arrow in the chest.

Want is the seed; dream is the tree;
the fruit is the life you dared to grow.
Water the want before it withers.

Somewhere a light is lit for the thing you'll be.
Walk toward it, though the road is dark;
the dark is only the unhired half of dawn.

Every building stood first as a thought;
every thought, as a wish someone kept.
Keep the wish; the walls will follow.

Dream in decades, act in days.
The oak does not hurry the acorn;
the acorn, nonetheless, becomes the oak.

They told the moon it was impossible to reach;
the moon said nothing and waited for the foot.
Impossible is only a slow possible.

An empty chair is not a lack;
it is the space a guest may fill,
or the silence you learn to keep.

Some of us are books no one has opened;
the words are no less true for being unread.
Open yourself, and the reader appears.

The desert within is not a wasteland;
it is where the small, green truth can grow
unseen by any crowd.

I missed the last train and found the night;
not lost, but lent an hour
no timetable ever gave.
